     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"With no defences, exfiltration is reachable. phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. pivot_internal then gives reach_internal, since the network is not segmented. From there the chain is auth_appserver, kerberoast_dc (stolen_admin), auth_dc, escalate_dc (admin_dc), dump_dbadmin_dc (stolen_dbadmin), auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So 0 controls is not enough. Both exfiltration routes (DB and fileserver) need stolen_dbadmin, which only dump_dbadmin_dc provides. That technique needs admin_dc, which needs foothold_dc. The only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks foothold_dc, then admin_dc, then stolen_dbadmin, then both footholds and both exfiltration techniques. Minimum = 1.\"}"
